---
title: Oatmeal Chocolate Chip Greek Yogurt Muffins
servings: 12
cuisine: american
main_protein: dairy
prep_time: "15 minutes"
cook_time: "18 minutes"
tags:
  - breakfast
  - oats
  - chocolate
  - yogurt
source: https://thebakermama.com/recipes/oatmeal-chocolate-chip-greek-yogurt-muffins/
image: ../obsidian/attachments/Oatmeal-Chocolate-Chip-Greek-Yogurt-Muffins.jpeg
leftover_portions: 8
prep:
  - Preheat oven to 350°F
  - Grease a 12-cup muffin pan with cooking spray
  - Measure out the streusel ingredients
---

Preheat #oven{} to 350°F. Grease a #12-cup muffin pan{} with cooking spray.

Whisk together @whole wheat flour{1%cup}, @old-fashioned oats{1.5%cups}, @baking powder{1.5%tsp}, @baking soda{1%tsp}, @salt{0.5%tsp}, and @cinnamon{1%tsp} in a #large bowl{}.

In a #medium bowl{}, whisk together @canola oil{0.25%cup}, @brown sugar{0.5%cup}, @eggs{2}, @vanilla extract{1%tsp}, and @vanilla greek yogurt{1%cup}. Combine wet and dry ingredients until incorporated. Fold in @semi-sweet chocolate chips{1%cup}.

Divide batter evenly among muffin cups, filling almost full.

Mix streusel ingredients (@canola oil{2%tbsp}, @brown sugar{0.33%cup}, @old-fashioned oats{0.5%cup}, @semi-sweet chocolate chips{0.33%cup}) with a fork until coated. Place a heaping tablespoon over each muffin.

Bake ~{15%minutes} until golden brown. Cool in pan ~{5%minutes} before transferring to a #wire rack{}.
